# Copy to .env.local (already gitignored) to enable optional cloud
# features in development. The app runs fully offline/local-first with
# both of these unset — see supabase/README.md's "Local development"
# section. Neither value below is a secret:
#
# - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is your project's public API endpoint.
# - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY holds your project's PUBLISHABLE key
#   (Dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys, starts with
#   sb_publishable_). The variable keeps its historical name, but the
#   legacy JWT-based "anon" key (starts with eyJ) is no longer accepted:
#   the app treats it as invalid configuration and stays in local mode.
#   The publishable key is designed to be shipped in client code; it is
#   meaningless without the Row Level Security policies in
#   supabase/migrations/ enforcing access.
#
# The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix means Expo inlines these into the JS bundle at
# build time (babel-preset-expo does this automatically) — anything with
# this prefix is public by definition, so NEVER put a secret here.
#
# NEVER put a secret key (sb_secret_...) or the legacy service_role key in
# this file or in any EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable. Secret keys bypass Row Level
# Security entirely and must never exist in client code. The only server
# code that uses one is the delete-account Edge Function, which receives
# it from Supabase's own function environment (SUPABASE_SECRET_KEYS) — it
# is never stored in this repository.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-publishable-key
